# {client-name} Brand Tokens

Read `.cursor/skills/{client-slug}-brand/SKILL.md` for full brand context. This rule enforces tokens in code.

## CSS variables (required)

Define these in your global stylesheet or `:root`. Use semantic names — never hardcode hex in components.

```css
:root {
  /* Colors — from approved palette */
  --color-bg-primary: {hex};
  --color-bg-secondary: {hex};
  --color-text-primary: {hex};
  --color-text-muted: {hex};
  --color-accent: {hex};
  --color-accent-secondary: {hex};

  /* Typography */
  --font-display: "{display-font}", {fallbacks};
  --font-body: "{body-font}", {fallbacks};
  --font-caption: "{caption-font}", {fallbacks};

  /* Spacing rhythm */
  --space-section: {e.g. 120px};
  --space-block: {e.g. 48px};
}
```

## Rules

1. **No hardcoded hex** in component files — use `var(--color-*)` only.
2. **No generic SaaS fonts** unless the project brand skill explicitly allows them.
3. **CTA copy** must match the approved table in the brand skill — not "Sign Up" or "Join Now" unless approved.
4. **Motion:** prefer CSS transitions 400–800ms ease; avoid bouncy/spring defaults on luxury/editorial projects.
5. **Images:** full-bleed heroes use `object-fit: cover`; never stretch logos.

## When tokens change

Update this file and `.cursor/skills/{client-slug}-brand/SKILL.md` together via `website-brand-foundation` iteration mode.
